  },
  "message": "fix(llms): don't stack the SDK's retries on rate-limit replays\n\nrun_with_rate_limit_retry replays a throttled call up to three times, and\neach replay went out with the provider SDK's own retries still enabled\n(max_retries defaults to 2), so one 429 turned into 3x3 requests on the\nwire and 3x3x3 once the agent-level retry is included: 27 byte-identical\nrequests for a single call in the benchmark.\n\nMark the attempts that replay an already-failed call and let the OpenAI\nprovider build its client with max_retries=0 for those. The first attempt\nstill uses the SDK's retries.",
  "parents": [
