    "body": "### Description\n\nOn `crewai==1.15.28`, one `429` from the provider produced **27 identical HTTP requests in 27.3 s**. Same\nbody, same tools, same user agent, none of them streamed. Three retry layers are nested and their counts\nmultiply:\n\n| layer | where (current `main`, `dec075b`) | factor |\n|---|---|---|\n| OpenAI SDK retries | `lib/crewai/src/crewai/llms/providers/openai/completion.py:377` (`max_retries: int = 2`) | ×3 |\n| CrewAI rate-limit retry | `lib/crewai/src/crewai/llms/retry.py:35` (`_LLM_RATE_LIMIT_MAX_ATTEMPTS = 3`), installed by the `call`/`acall` wrapper in `lib/crewai/src/crewai/llms/base_llm.py:201` and `:215` | ×3 |\n| Agent-level retry | `lib/crewai/src/crewai/agent/core.py:301-304` (`max_retry_limit` default `2`) → `_check_execution_error` `:886-887` → `_handle_execution_error` `:909` re-enters `execute_task` | ×3 |\n\n3 × 3 × 3 = 27, and the request log matches that shape exactly.\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. `crewai==1.15.28`, Python 3.12, a single agent with one tool.\n2. Point the LLM at an OpenAI-compatible server that always answers `429` (bench cell `crewai/429` in\n   https://github.com/simin-yuan/agent-double-exec-bench — the cell and the raw request log are both in\n   that repo).\n3. Run one task.\n4. Count the requests the server sees: **27**, over 27.3 s.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nOne user-visible call should spend a number of requests bounded by the *largest* of the three budgets,\nnot by their product — and the outermost retry should wait before it re-sends.\n\n### Screenshots/Code snippets\n\nThe three places, on `main`:\n\n```python\n# completion.py:377\nmax_retries: int = 2\n\n# retry.py:35\n_LLM_RATE_LIMIT_MAX_ATTEMPTS = 3\n\n# agent/core.py:301-304\nmax_retry_limit: int | None = None\n...\nself.max_retry_limit = max_retry_limit if max_retry_limit is not None else 2\n\n# agent/core.py:874 — the comment that states the re-entry outright\n# A retry re-enters execute_task, which opens a new agent_execution_started scope\n```\n\n### Operating System\n\nWindows 11\n\n### Python Version\n\n3.12\n\n### crewAI Version\n\n1.15.28 (request log). The source locations above were read on `main` @ `dec075b`.\n\n### crewAI Tools Version\n\nNot involved — the tool in the repro is a local counter, no `crewai-tools` package.\n\n### Virtual Environment\n\nvenv\n\n### Evidence\n\nFrom `results/e1/crewai/429/server.jsonl` (27 lines):\n\n- all `POST /v1/chat/completions`, `stream=false`, identical body hash (`b7c7a67c…`), identical UA\n  (`OpenAI/Python 2.54.0`)\n- the SDK's own counter cycles 0 → 1 → 2, nine times (`x-stainless-retry-count` = `0,1,2, 0,1,2, …`)\n- gaps inside a group: 1.0–1.06 s; gaps between groups: 1.11–1.92 s, **except two of them: 0.02 s and\n  0.03 s** — that is the agent layer, which re-enters `execute_task` with no backoff at all\n- the call ends in `openai.RateLimitError`\n\n**The second layer does not always engage**, which matters if you tune this by hand. Same cell family:\n**9** requests for `429-hard` and `500-text-429`, but **27** for `429`, `429-neutral-body` and\n`500-ratelimit-text`. `_ThrottlingErrorClassifier` decides which of the two you get, so changing\n`max_retry_limit` alone adjusts one of three budgets that only sometimes apply.\n\n### Possible Solution\n\nKeep the SDK's retries on the first attempt and turn them off on CrewAI's own replays — the provider builds\nits client with `with_options(max_retries=0)` when the current attempt is a replay of a call that already\nfailed. The first attempt keeps the SDK's three tries, so nothing is lost on a transient blip. Expected on\nthe same cell: 3 × (3 + 1 + 1) = **15** requests instead of 27.\n\nThis does not remove the agent-level multiplication (the 0.02 s re-sends). Whether a failed task should\nre-call the model at all is a design question, so it is reported here rather than patched.\n\n### Additional context\n\n**`_times_executed` is never reset.** `agent/core.py:242` declares\n`_times_executed: int = PrivateAttr(default=0)`; `:886-887` increments it and compares it against\n`max_retry_limit`. Nothing resets it when a task succeeds, so `max_retry_limit` is a budget for the *agent\nobject's whole lifetime*, not per task — an agent that has already retried once pays for that on every\nlater task. (This overlaps with #5822, which mentions the same non-reset while fixing #5802. It is listed\nhere because it is a separate defect and the two fixes do not conflict.)\n\n**Not the same as:**\n\n- **#5802 / #5822 / #6048** — a *tool* runs twice after a retry (idempotency guard). Here the *LLM\n  request* is sent 27 times; no tool needs to be involved at all.\n- **#7449** — same \"two retry paths multiply\" shape, but in `ToolUsage._use`/`_ause`, i.e. the tool path,\n  not the provider call.\n- **#6639** — flow-level `retry_count` persisting across `kickoff()` calls; same failure mode as\n  `_times_executed`, different object.\n\n---\n\nDisclosure: I directed this work. The source reading, the patch, its tests and the measurements were\nproduced by AI assistants I operate. Every number above comes from the server logs in\nagent-double-exec-bench, and I will answer review comments on it.\n\nPer CONTRIBUTING this should carry the `llm-generated` label; I'll add it if my account can, otherwise\nplease apply it.\n",
